      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_h043"
      ],
      "explanation": "A logarithm asks which exponent produces the stated number. Since \\(8^{1/3}=2\\) and \\(2^3=8\\),\n\\[\n\\log_8 2=\\frac13,\n\\qquad\n\\log_2 8=3.\n\\]\nSubstituting these values gives\n\\[\nx=\\left(\\frac13\\right)^3\n=\\frac1{27}=3^{-3}.\n\\]\nThis value of \\(x\\) is positive, so its logarithm is defined. Because \\(3^{-3}=x\\), we obtain \\(\\log_3 x=\\boxed{-3}\\), choice A.",
      "id": "logarithm-definition",
      "sourceRef": "amc/1966_AMC_12_Q09#logarithm-definition",
      "title": "Read logarithms as exponents"
    }
